      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "I am being highly cautious because in kidney disease, even small amounts of supplemental minerals can pose serious risks. High potassium levels (hyperkalemia) can severely affect heart rhythm, which is an immediate danger. Please understand that I cannot give medical permission, and self-treating is unsafe when kidney function is compromised. For immediate relief until your appointment, try focusing on staying well-hydrated with approved fluids and gently stretching, and call your doctor's on-call service to discuss this urgent symptom.",
